# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TATS .gitignore
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Anything below is either build / editor noise OR could contain live
# captured tokens, decoded JWT claims, or user-identifying information
# that must never make it into a public release. When in doubt: don't
# commit it.


# ---- Python bytecode / build artifacts ------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyd
*.pyo
*.so

# Setuptools / wheel builds
*.egg
*.egg-info/
*.whl
build/
dist/
pip-wheel-metadata/
MANIFEST

# ---- Virtual environments -------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env
.env.*
.python-version

# ---- Testing / coverage / typecheck / lint --------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.pyright/
pyrightconfig.local.json
.ruff_cache/
*.log
*.log.*

# ---- Editors / IDEs -------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.\#*
\#*\#

# ---- OS metadata ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db

# ---- Claude Code local settings -------------------------------------------
# Personal per-machine permissions / paths. .claude/settings.json (no
# ".local" suffix) may be shared intentionally; the ".local.*" variants
# never should.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/**/*.local.*
.claude/projects/


# ===========================================================================
# TATS-specific sensitive artifacts
# ===========================================================================
# Everything below can carry real access / refresh / id tokens, decoded
# JWT claim contents (oid, sub, upn, email, tid), or full replayable
# request bodies — treat every match as a wholesale credential dump.

# ---- SQLite databases -----------------------------------------------------
# tats writes tokens.db by default; live cdp / mitm captures dump into
# whatever -o names. Contents include JWT payloads and (with
# --store-tokens) full raw tokens.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---- Raw traffic captures -------------------------------------------------
# Burp "Save items" XML exports and mitmproxy flow files hold complete
# request/response bodies including any bearer tokens in transit. HAR
# and pcap files are the same risk from other tools.
*.mitm
*.har
*.pcap
*.pcapng

# Allowlist the small synthetic fixtures shipped for tests + demos. They
# are generated by examples/make_*.py and contain only fabricated tokens
# — no real user data.
!examples/fixture.mitm
!examples/fixture.xml

# Any *.xml at the repo root is almost certainly a real Burp export.
/*.xml

# ---- Token exports (dashboard downloads / API responses) ------------------
# The dashboard's Copy/Download buttons and /api/export produce files
# in these shapes. All carry full raw tokens when --store-tokens was on.
token-*.json
tokens-export-*.json
roadtx-*.json
*.roadtools_auth
.roadtools_auth

# ---- Live-capture Chrome profile temp dirs --------------------------------
# --launch-chrome makes a throwaway profile under $TEMP; if it ever
# lands next to the repo (e.g. TMPDIR override) the browser session
# state is inside.
tats-cdp-profile-*/
btt-cdp-profile-*/

# ---- Entrascopes enrichment cache -----------------------------------------
# The 500-KB apps/resources JSON is cached under $TATS_CACHE. Only
# matters if someone points the cache at the repo root, but harmless
# to ignore.
tats-cache/
.tats-cache/


# ===========================================================================
# Ad-hoc scratch / smoke-test scripts and their outputs
# ===========================================================================
# Legitimate unit tests live in tests/ and stay tracked. The patterns
# below only match at the *repo root* (leading /) so they can't hide
# a genuine test file from the suite.

# One-off scripts developers accumulate during research sessions.
/scratch*.py
/scratch/
/tmp/
/_scratch*.py
/_leak*.py
/_trace*.py
/try*.py
/try_*.py
/smoke*.py
/repro*.py
/debug*.py

# Root-level "test_*.py" is almost certainly a scratch script — real
# tests belong under tests/.
/test_*.py

# Scratch DBs / XMLs I've made during development sessions.
/exp*.db
/perf*.db
/mig*.db
/e2e*.db
/synth*.db
/synth*.xml
/tokens.db

# Screenshots / clipboard drops / notes.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.bmp
*.tiff
# ...but keep the roseart-style diagrams in the README/examples if any
# get added later:
!examples/**/*.png
!examples/**/*.gif
NOTES.md
notes.md
TODO.md
todo.md
